0,Benue–Congo languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benue–Congo_languages,"Benue–Congo is a major branch of the Volta-Congo languages which covers most of Sub-Saharan Africa.The neighbouring Volta–Niger branch of Nigeria and Benin is sometimes called ""West Benue–Congo"", but it does not form a united branch with Benue–Congo.",Iguta,Niger-Congo
1,"Iguta Language (NAR) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/nar/,Iguta is an endangered indigenous language of Nigeria. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. The language is used as a first language by some people in every generation of the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Iguta,Niger-Congo
2,Iguta - nar (Niger-Congo) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/nar/,"Iguta (nar) is part of the Niger-Congo family and Niger-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Volta-Congo, Benue-Congo, Kainji, Eastern, Northern Jos, Jera class. Iguta speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts",Iguta,Niger-Congo
3,Iguta / Anaguta,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Iguta.htm,"Other comments: Iguta or Anaguta, Eguta, Guta, Naraguta, Narkuta is spoken by approximately 10,000 speakers in Bauchi state: Toro LGA; Plateau state: Bassa, Jos-North, and Jos-East LGAs, Nigeria. Iguta has a traditional duodecimal numeral system.",Iguta,Niger-Congo
4,Process: Case of Suffixation and Prefixation in Iguta,https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/ecc9/871be54e8c0f9ee4b90f6425bde7b123efa9.pdf,"Genetically, Iguta is a “Group 1” of the seven Benue-Congo language families under Niger-Kordofanian phylum (Greenberg, 1963). Iguta is dialectally diverse, with at least five recorded dialects being in used with mutual intelligibility existing among them.",Iguta,Niger-Congo
5,"Nigeria people groups, languages and religions | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/countries/NI,"Maps, charts and statistics of Nigeria ethnic people groups, languages and religions. Sortable and downloadable Nigeria data.",Iguta,Niger-Congo
6,The numeral system of Proto-Niger-Congo,https://library.oapen.org/bitstream/handle/20.500.12657/28278/1001684.pdf?sequence=1,"1.1 Niger-Congo: the state of research and the prospects for reconstruction. 1.2 Sources and the monograph structure.ately apparent. On the other hand, some of the forms placed in separate columns might be etymologically related (e.g. dɨɨn Giro and dínkā Iguta).",Iguta,Niger-Congo
7,Niger-Congo languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/niger-congo-languages/,"The Niger-Congo family counts between 1 300 and 1 500 languages, depending on the classifications, representing alone nearly a quarter of the planet’s languages.",Iguta,Niger-Congo
